<h2 class="vt">Hi, I'm Nick.</h2>
<p>I take messy operational problems apart and rebuild them as clean, step-by-step systems. I like owning the work directly: no black-box retainers, no software you don't need.</p>
</div>
<p style="margin: 16px 0 0 0">I'm a real person, not an agency. A few things that shape how I work:</p>
<ul style="margin: 8px 0 0 0; padding-left: 18px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<li><b style="color: #FFE2B0">Autodidact &amp; jack of all trades.</b> If I don't know it, I'll find it and learn it. My ADHD brain is wired for deep research and pattern recognition: give me an unfamiliar stack or a gnarly operational problem and I'll dig until I have the answer.</li>
<li><b style="color: #FFE2B0">Martial philosophy.</b> 2nd-degree black belt and former instructor in Hwa Rang Do. Years of training taught me discipline, precision, and how to stay calm when things break under pressure.</li>
<li><b style="color: #FFE2B0">Audiophile &amp; drum &amp; bass DJ.</b> I care about clean signal chains and sound: mixing DnB on Traktor, playing keys, and dialing in studio audio. That same attention to detail carries straight into my code and systems.</li>
<li><b style="color: #FFE2B0">Competitive gamer &amp; live streamer.</b> I play to win, and I built my own Twitch production rig on OBS and Streamer.bot with automated scenes, alerts, and chat, running 30 days straight, live every day.</li>
<li><b style="color: #FFE2B0">Precision and care.</b> I build my own PCs, shoot color-calibrated fine-art photography, stretch canvases, and cook. I sweat the small stuff most people skip.</li>
</ul>
<p style="margin: 16px 0 0 0; color: #A8742A">Based in the SF Bay Area with my wife and our two dogs. Off the clock, I'm usually queuing into a competitive match or catching up on anime.</p>
